# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in the keys you want to enable.  # Instruction line 1: how to use this file.
# Every key is OPTIONAL: QuizForge Otari Edition runs its full loop on the offline heuristic engine
# plus labeled STUB comparison answers with no keys at all. Stub mode is honest by design.
# --- Mozilla Otari gateway (the Otari Edition model layer) ---  # Section: Otari.
# HONEST STATE (2026-11-02): the gateway's exact base URL and model slugs were NOT verified live
# (the onboarding doc fetch failed from this environment). Confirm them against
# https://www.otari.ai/devs-wilding BEFORE relying on live mode. The client assumes an
# OpenAI-compatible POST {base}/chat/completions with a Bearer key; if the doc shows a
# different path, set OTARI_CHAT_PATH to match.
# The Otari API key — free signup at https://otari.ai. Never committed, never shared.  # The gateway credential.
OTARI_API_KEY=
# The Otari gateway base URL, e.g. the root the onboarding doc lists (no trailing slash).  # The gateway endpoint.
OTARI_BASE_URL=
# The two open-weight model slugs to compare, exactly as Otari names them.  # The comparison pair.
OTARI_MODEL_A=
OTARI_MODEL_B=
# The chat path, only needed if the onboarding doc shows a non-default route.  # Default: /chat/completions.
# OTARI_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
# --- Everything below is inherited unchanged from QuizForge Live (optional) ---  # Section: inherited.
# Nightshift (primary Nemotron route for the Live loop): local-only software, see Live README.
# METERLESS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088/v1
# METERLESS_RUNTIME_TOKEN=
# METERLESS_MODEL=meterless/auto
# OpenRouter fallback for the Live loop (verified free-tier seat).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Zetaris AI Data Harness (preflight-gated until an instance exists).
# ZETARIS_REST_URL=
# ZETARIS_API_KEY=
# ZETARIS_ORG_ID=1
